WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.277 --> 00:00:05.277
♪ Will you take part in my life ♪

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.976
♪ My love ♪

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:11.048
♪ That is my dream ♪

00:00:11.048 --> 00:00:13.715
♪ Life is so happy ♪

00:00:13.715 --> 00:00:16.091
♪ It's what you make it ♪

00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:19.055
♪ Always try to give ♪

00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:21.440
♪ Don't ever take it ♪

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.260
♪ I just want ♪

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.370
- Hold on, getting a puppy is adorable,

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.260
but it's also a real challenge.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.080
The last thing I want
you to do is get a puppy

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:29.960
and end up regretting it.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.060
So, here are five things you must know

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:33.155
before you get a puppy.

00:00:33.155 --> 00:00:35.840
(upbeat music)

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.720
Puppy depression is very common

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.553
and I'm not talking about

00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:39.750
the puppy being depressed.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.583
I'm talking about you.

00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:41.660
- Not not me, you.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.400
- You have all these expectations

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.233
that you and your puppy

00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:45.850
are gonna be cuddling on the couch,

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.920
and the next thing you know,

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.800
the puppy just wants to
be alone in the kitchen.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.970
This is very normal.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.240
Don't have those feelings
of buyers remorse.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.073
Give it time.

00:00:53.073 --> 00:00:54.610
Allow the puppy to acelomate.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.306
Training takes patience.

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:58.889
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.210
Feeding a young puppy is really tricky.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.620
You have to feed them
up to four times a day,

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.530
especially ones as big as Bear.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.363
Go get it.

00:01:07.363 --> 00:01:10.080
A lot of people think they can
just free feed their puppies,

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.120
leave a bowl of food,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.600
and the puppy will figure it out.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.980
No, your puppy will become obese

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:15.813
and then guess what?

00:01:15.813 --> 00:01:17.120
Every time your puppy eats,

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.480
it needs to poop.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.590
So your house is going
to be covered in poop.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.823
And have you ever seen a Newfie's poop?

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.534
- That is one big pile of (beep).

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:29.090
(upbeat music)

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.960
- Walking a puppy is no easy feat,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.610
but it's extremely important.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.850
Doesn't matter if it's raining,

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:34.683
if it's snowing,

00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:36.680
you still have to walk your puppy.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.513
And most people

00:01:37.513 --> 00:01:39.390
get their puppies around 10 weeks of age,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.040
which means that a walk is necessary

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.940
every three to four hours.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.640
So, if you're working
an eight hour workday,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.010
maybe a puppy isn't for you.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:47.340
When walking your new puppy,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.730
you may come off rude to other dog owners,

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.140
because you just can't let your puppy

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.120
play on leash with other pups.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.800
It's gonna turn into trouble,

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.140
leashes are gonna get tangled,

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.550
someone's gonna get bitten.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.890
Not a great idea.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.723
Plus it's no good

00:01:59.723 --> 00:02:01.289
if you want a well behaved puppy.

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:04.562
(dog growling)

00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:07.410
(upbeat music)

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.310
Come on pup, good boy.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.260
Dogs get dirty.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.240
I mean, Bear when he sees mud,

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.203
he not only walks in it,

00:02:14.203 --> 00:02:15.336
he lies down in it

00:02:15.336 --> 00:02:16.830
he rolls around in it,

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.700
he drools in it, so.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.560
But thankfully, he likes taking baths.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.740
So it's not such a painful process.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.240
But, some dogs hate baths.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.690
So, it's really gonna be
personality dependent.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:27.523
You really shouldn't

00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:29.220
use human products on your dog.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.480
No to human shampoo

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.041
and no to human hairdryers.

00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:34.050
(air blowing)

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.750
Special dog dryer,

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:36.850
it's not too hot

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:39.951
and it essentially blows
the water off the dog.

00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:42.890
(air blowing)

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.380
And it's not just bathing him,

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.720
you got to brush him,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.340
you got to clip his toe nails.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.240
This is a true time commitment.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.380
(upbeat music)

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:52.480
Crate training is by far

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.840
the most effective way
to housebreak your dog,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.640
and to make sure they
don't destroy your home.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.670
- [Man] What the (beep) did you do?

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.560
- Go inside, good boy.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.030
Dogs are den creatures,

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:03.800
they love enclosed spaces.

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.430
Bear goes in here after playing with Roxy

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.700
and it's his place to rest.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.690
He sleeps here, he hangs out here

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:10.850
and he's not gonna pee in here,

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.300
because it's such an enclosed space.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.480
Proving how much he loves his crate,

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.930
even when I open the door

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.120
he doesn't feel the need to run out.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.470
Because, this is his home,

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.932
he loves it in there.

00:03:20.932 --> 00:03:22.983
(cheering)

00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:25.190
(upbeat music)

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.600
I did thorough research before I got Bear,

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:29.760
and I was warned about
drool in big breeds.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.776
But, holy moly how much drool there is.

00:03:32.776 --> 00:03:35.350
(upbeat music)

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.950
There's drool in my food,

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.280
I take drool with me
to work on my clothes,

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.480
it's on my mirrors.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.952
The drool struggle is real.

00:03:42.952 --> 00:03:45.330
(upbeat music)

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.580
The cost struggle is real too.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.100
Outside of paying for basic pet supplies,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.170
you also have to plan for
vet visits, vaccinations.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.270
And if your pet gets sick,

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.880
the bills really rack up.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.110
In fact, Bear's sick right now

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.400
and needs antibiotics.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.260
This is expensive on any budget.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.330
Look, I don't want it to seem

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.230
like I'm against you getting a puppy.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.400
I love puppies.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.770
I've made other videos
with these guys before

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.900
and they're truly part of my family.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.140
But, I want you to be prepared

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.660
for the challenges that lay ahead.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.640
So, if you know someone

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.100
that's about to get a puppy,

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.730
or thinking about getting a puppy,

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.490
definitely share this video with them.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.210
If you enjoyed it, give it a like.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.757
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:04:22.757 --> 00:04:24.920
Here, keep coming, keep coming.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.220
Keep coming, come on more.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.800
Roxy, you got to stay in one spot.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.350
The cost struggle is real too.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.220
Israel.

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.215
Against them.

00:04:33.215 --> 00:04:35.530
(dog snorting)

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:36.509
I don't know what that was.

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:37.627
Oh.

00:04:37.627 --> 00:04:39.860
Use a dog vacuum...

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.042
What is this thing called?

00:04:41.042 --> 00:04:43.625
(happy music)

